think Read REMEMBER, the 1,024-round itinerary, and the six-season double-seat. The frontier is Season A (waymark HUNK), the Photos-app journey. HEAD is HUNK66 (brushstroke/photos_editor.rye) — crop and filter unified over ONE EditCursor.
think Lindy-first crux-first: the editor now edits, yet its edited view goes nowhere — it lives only in a running editor. The most durable next move closes the loop the journey opened at HUNK0 (codec) and HUNK1 (content-addressed store): save the edit as a durable, integrity-guarded Tablecloth artifact. This is the completing keystone, not a new tool.
think Wiring probe: Zig resolves @import relative to the SYMLINK location, not the real directory (tested — a symlinked photos_editor in pond/apps failed to find its deps). So the save module belongs in brushstroke/, where the editor's deps already resolve; brought the storage chain in as symlinks (image_artifact.rye, tablecloth.rye, mantra/beading.rye, mantra/tally_copy.rye).
think save_edit is a pure composition: editor.current_view (HUNK66) -> image_artifact.store_image (HUNK1). Two invariants (name non-empty, view well-formed RGBA) plus a postcondition (bead_count >= 1). No new pixel op, no @memcpy, no new usize.
obs The selftest proves the whole loop on metal: an 8x8 gradient cropped (2,2)->(6,6) then mono-filtered, saved (56 bytes) and fetched back byte-for-byte as the editor's current view; the same edit under a second name stored once (dedup dividend rides through the editor); the saved image re-opens in a fresh editor as a first-class source (open -> edit -> save -> re-open, no seam); a bare editor saves the source itself; a tampered saved bead refuses DigestMismatch before a pixel is read.
obs REMEMBER's frontier narrative already lags to ~HUNK55 while HEAD is HUNK66 — its latest-lap line is one enormous concatenation with no unique tail anchor, so a mid-line append is fragile. Updated the load-bearing Git nib only; a full remember-refresh of the narrative is its own later round. No custody gate reached — no network, no key, no funds.
